1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,500
A bio fertilizer is different.

2
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:08,033
It is a culture of living microbes that make nutrients available to the plant.

3
00:00:08,033 --> 00:00:15,963
Rhizobium in legume nodules, and Frankia in the roots of our own utis tree, fix nitrogen from the air.

4
00:00:15,963 --> 00:00:24,570
Azolla, a tiny water fern carrying the cyanobacterium Anabaena, is the classic bio fertilizer of rice fields.

5
00:00:24,570 --> 00:00:28,958
Azotobacter fixes nitrogen free in the soil.

6
00:00:28,958 --> 00:00:32,513
Some bacteria dissolve locked up phosphate.

7
00:00:32,513 --> 00:00:37,565
And mycorrhizal fungi extend the root system for phosphorus and water.

